<article class="env-lemma" id="00P2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00P2">Lemma <span data-tag="00P2">10.116.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $S' \to S$ be a surjection of finite type $k$ algebras. Let $\mathfrak p \subset S$ be a prime ideal, and let $\mathfrak p'$ be the corresponding prime ideal of $S'$. Let $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S)$, resp. $X' = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S')$, and let $x \in X$, resp. $x'\in X'$ be the point corresponding to $\mathfrak p$, resp. $\mathfrak p'$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _{x'} X' - \dim _ x X = \text{height}(\mathfrak p') - \text{height}(\mathfrak p).  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/00P1" data-tag="00P1">10.116.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>